type: software
title: "Relativity leaves only the symmetric potentials integrable: a classification of homogeneous polynomial potentials for the additive relativistic Hamiltonian"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. For H = sqrt(1 + p1^2 + p2^2) + V(q1, q2) with V a nonzero real homogeneous polynomial of degree k >= 3, H has a second first integral, meromorphic on the natural complex phase space and independent of H, if and only if, after a rotation, V = c q1^k or (k even) V = c (q1^2 + q2^2)^(k/2). The result is new for k >= 6; for k = 3, 4, 5 Przybylska, Szuminski and Maciejewski (2023) reached it by another route. Complex-coefficient potentials with a nonisotropic linear factor and isotropic multiplicities different from k/2 are integrable only when they are a power of one nonisotropic linear form; in particular generic potentials are non-integrable, which proves the stated consequence of the 2023 conjecture. Isotropic monomials and the exact-half multiplicity case remain open."
